  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 items, 3 patients). Two decisions changed when new results arrived while I was working.\n\n• Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: I first renewed it for 90 days and ordered a BMP, because the August potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample and doesn't count. Then an outside BMP from 10/20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001); the old order mr-00283 stays stopped. Urgent review task to you (task-t0013), corrected reply sent to the patient, note written. The BMP order (sr-t0002) is still open. His hernia repair is set for 11/12.\n• Samuel Price (pt-0030):\n  – Lisinopril 20 mg: renewed at first, then the lab corrected his 10/06 creatinine from 1.36 to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase, which the protocol treats like a high potassium. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003); mr-00295 stays stopped. Urgent review task to you (task-t0014). He says he is out of the 20 mg.\n  – Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58 after the correction, and his outside HbA1c of 7.1% (8/19) is within 6 months. That one order covers his portal request and both pharmacy requests.\n  – He got a corrected reply, and I wrote a note.\n• Marcus Webb (pt-0031):\n  – Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0005), and a BMP ordered (sr-t0006). His last BMP was 10/20/2025, more than 12 months ago, and he had a visit on 9/28/2026. A potassium of 4.6 alone arrived today; it isn't a BMP, so the decision stands.\n  – Metformin 500 mg twice daily: 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was entered in error (mislabelled specimen); the valid eGFR is 92 and his HbA1c is 6.9% (9/28).\n  – He got a reply, and I wrote a note.\n\nStill open in your results queue (I didn't touch it): three new items for these patients that I reviewed and acted on (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004), plus earlier items. Those include critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3, task-00011) and pt-0008 (6.4, task-00005) that need your attention today.",
